  "limitations": [
    "The study used a fictitious employee in the performance appraisal task, with only one gender represented on the ratee side, limiting conclusive data about the halo effect.",
    "The exposure time for lighting conditions (around 85 minutes for mood measurement) might not be sufficient for all emotional responses, especially for indirect effects of lighting.",
    "The low CRI conditions in Experiment 2 might not have been distinct enough (or had other unknown characteristics) to produce a gender difference on room light evaluations.",
    "The room light at low CRI did not produce appropriate context cues to enhance long-term recall and recognition processes, suggesting a limitation in the generalizability of memory findings across CRI levels."
